This package installs Intel's libcamhal and the ipu6, ipu6ep and ipu6epmtl
plugins. The adaptor selects the plugin from the IPU PCI device ID; Raptor
Lake uses ipu6ep. Camera configuration is installed under /etc/camera/.

This is a separate camera stack from libcamera. Installing it does not make
libcamera's simple pipeline use the IPU6 PSYS hardware, and does not change
an existing v4l2-relayd configuration using libcamerasrc.

Runtime requirements:
- A compatible Intel IPU6 PSYS kernel driver, in addition to ISYS and the
  camera sensor driver. The existing sys-kernel/ipu6-drivers package can
  provide the out-of-tree PSYS driver, subject to kernel compatibility.
- IPU6 firmware, provided by sys-kernel/linux-firmware. The camera-bins
  dependency installs userspace libraries and headers, not firmware.
- Sensor/module configuration supported by Intel's HAL.

For GStreamer, Intel's icamerasrc plugin (icamerasrc_slim_api branch) must be
installed separately. It uses libcamhal, whereas libcamerasrc uses libcamera.
Test the new stack before switching a working v4l2-relayd service to
icamerasrc; do not use both stacks on the same camera at the same time.
